1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,065
Let’s look under the hood.

2
00:00:03,065 --> 00:00:09,700
Before changing code, identify the main components and who owns each responsibility.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,522
This Nx monorepo contains two applications, shared libraries, and tools.

4
00:00:15,522 --> 00:00:19,700
Separate application logic, shared presentation, and source analysis.

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:27,200
Invoicing manages invoices, with its own entry point, routes, list, and detail pages.

6
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:32,333
Procurement manages purchase orders through its own entry and routes.

7
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:34,700
Both applications use shared libraries.

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,752
This is the real Invoicing App.

9
00:00:37,752 --> 00:00:44,700
The router selects pages; App owns invoice state and passes it to the pages that need it.

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:50,522
The Design System supplies the shell, fields, tables, and dialogs.

11
00:00:50,522 --> 00:00:54,700
One shared component can therefore affect both applications.

12
00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:00,742
Shared contains business types, fixtures, totals, money formatting, and local storage.

13
00:01:00,742 --> 00:01:04,700
It also exports the locale and translation interface.

14
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,978
Locale, document direction, styling, and icon meaning are separate.

15
00:01:08,978 --> 00:01:14,700
Study uses document RTL and MUI LTR; icons require semantic review, not automatic mirroring.

16
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,718
The Scanner collects static evidence and potential risks.

17
00:01:18,718 --> 00:01:24,700
The Codemod constrains changes through safety checks; a finding is not automatic repair approval.

18
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:29,227
These relationships come from actual imports.

19
00:01:29,227 --> 00:01:33,809
Both applications use Design System and Shared.

20
00:01:33,809 --> 00:01:39,700
Tools analyze source files; neither application imports the other.

21
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:49,065
Our real example is invoice1048: Northstar Studio, four thousand eight hundred US dollars, Pending.

22
00:01:49,065 --> 00:01:54,700
The actual table link opens the same invoice details.

23
00:01:55,300 --> 00:02:02,564
A symptom may appear in an application while its owner is a shared component or runtime layer.

24
00:02:02,564 --> 00:02:04,700
Establish causality before changing code.

25
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:09,700
How do we find RTL risks across this codebase?
